too high the pattern "(a)|(b)" has no group 3: its groups are numbered 0 to 2, where 0 is the whole match
too high maybe the pattern "(a)|(b)" has no group 3: its groups are numbered 0 to 2, where 0 is the whole match
negative the pattern "(a)|(b)" has no group -1: its groups are numbered 0 to 2, where 0 is the whole match
no groups the pattern "x" has no group 1: its only group is 0, the whole match
no names the pattern "(a)|(b)" has no group named "a": it has no named groups; write (?<name>...) to name one
unknown name the pattern "(?<month>\d{1,2})/(?<day>\d{1,2})/(?<year>\d{4})" has no group named "years": its named groups are "month", "day" and "year"
unknown maybe the pattern "(?<month>\d{1,2})/(?<day>\d{1,2})/(?<year>\d{4})" has no group named "": its named groups are "month", "day" and "year"
one name the pattern "(?<only>x)" has no group named "other": its one named group is "only"
two names the pattern "(?<one>x)(?<two>y)" has no group named "three": its named groups are "one" and "two"
unset name the group named "sign" in the pattern "(?<sign>-)?\d+" took no part in this match; use named_maybe("sign") to get nothing instead
unset name maybe nothing
